From 6947489a11906abb3782a4c766ede2c72b9f23de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ESP32S3VM coreclk <coreclk@esp32s3vm.invalid>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 11:52:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] hw: gate digital peripheral holds by the ESP32-S3 reset
 domain

GDMA, the interrupt matrix, UART, SPI1, TWAI and the AES/SHA/RSA/HMAC/DS
engines take a soc-reset link and skip their clearing hold phase when the
pending ESP32-S3 reset only covers a CPU (PROCPU/APPCPU). The blanket
QEMU device reset previously wiped this guest-visible state on every
reset request, which made the existing CPU-only software resets
destructive; the ESP32-S3 keeps digital peripherals alive across CPU
resets (TRM v1.8 ch.7 7.1). Machines without the link keep the previous
behavior.
---
